<h1>About</h1>
<p>An agent-governed pipeline system. AI agents are first-class users, operating under scoped permissions with full provenance on every write.</p>
<p>Its first piece is a job finder: it watches a chosen set of companies, reads their careers pages, and records whether each tracked role is still listed, through one audited write path. Every verdict says who wrote it and why.</p>
<p>A company or a role found elsewhere is added by its link: its careers page is found and read right away, and a role you add is tracked. A job board's link is never read; it is kept as where you found the role.</p>
<p>A search profile says what you are looking for. An agent of its own, the suggester, weighs every watched page's latest roles against it at no cost and proposes the ones that fit, each with why; it never proposes a role you track or dismissed, and only you track one. The Roles and Companies pages find a role by its title, company or place, and a company by its name, domain or a place it hires in; suggestions you don't want can be dismissed many at once.</p>
<p>An application starts from a role's page and moves through its stages on the Pipeline page, with what happened along the way. Only you start one or move it: no agent can, whatever it holds, and one that tries is refused on the record.</p>
<p>A role's description is read from its own page (through its board's job API, or the page rendered; never by the AI) when an application starts or when you ask, and every version is kept. Your resume is pasted on the Profile page and held in this database only.</p>
<p>From them, a draft agent writes a cover letter or a short outreach note for an application, in the role's language unless you ask for another. It claims only what your resume shows, names the lines of it the draft rests on, and lists what the role asks for that your resume doesn't show. You edit each draft and approve it on the application's page, then copy it and send it yourself: nothing is ever sent from here, and only you can edit or approve one.</p>
<p>Everything watched can be checked at once from the dashboard, its plan and the most it could cost shown first. What changed then lists what the check found: answers that changed, suggestions made and withdrawn, careers pages and boards, new questions, and lists that changed so much they may be another page now.</p>
<p>What an agent can't settle waits for you on the Review page: a careers page found at low confidence, a list read only in part, an answer resting on the AI's judgment alone. Each question comes with what was seen and an action proposed; you decide it, on the record. One you leave as is comes back only when what was seen changes.</p>
<p>Each agent run holds a credential issued for that run, with only the scopes it needs, and every write it makes is checked against it, down to what it changes: the verifier records verdicts but never tracks a role, and the suggester proposes roles but never touches one you decided on. A write no scope allows is refused, and the refusal is on the record. The Agents page shows who may write what, the credentials their runs held, and what each wrote.</p>
<p class="muted">Local and single-user: there is no login, so it is never deployed as it is.</p>
